# The fastest version benchmarked so far, one for each way (REQ14/SPEED-1).
# tools/speed-gate.sh builds the version named here and runs it turn and turn about with the
# version being landed, which must carry bytes at not less than 90% of its rate.
#
# A version is a commit of this repository, or "pf.7" for the fork at mosh-1.4.0-pf.7, which is
# where each way begins. When the gate finds the version being landed the faster of the two, it
# says so, and that version's commit is written here in the change that follows it (a commit
# cannot name itself). Two builds of the same code come out a few percent apart either way, so
# the name here may change with nothing gained; it names a version to compare with, not a figure.
#
# The ways are tools/speed.py's: udp (bytes through a TCP forward), stream (a copy over a
# stream), relay (a TCP forward with the session carried by the relays).
#
# way    version                                     when, and what was measured
udp      ad278156bc62cd7406cc86f9ea5169fb1577d5bc    2026-11-16: 106% of 6465584 by the gate (the names and the wire's last change; 48.2 against 45.7 Mbit/s)
stream   ad278156bc62cd7406cc86f9ea5169fb1577d5bc    2026-11-16: 100% of 6465584 by the gate, and the faster by its own measure (the names and the wire's last change; 40.5 against 40.5 Mbit/s)
relay    2b279d90b6fc686332c6044bb24c807313b08a67    2026-11-14: 323% of pf.7 by the gate (the relay carried; the gain is forwarding's, items 15 and 17; 45.5 against 14.1 Mbit/s)
